## Robot Asset Removal, 2026-09-07

Synria and Yahboom source geometry, vendor ROS packages, and derived conversions
were removed from the current tree. Flattened Robotiq geometry was also removed.
The [file-by-file manifest](docs/VENDOR_ASSET_REMOVAL.md) records provenance,
retained first-party layers, ambiguities, and history exposure.

**This corrects the previous redistribution posture.** Product ownership and a
non-commercial portfolio purpose were previously cited for including Yahboom
files; this repository no longer relies on that rationale. It also no longer
relies on Synria's email-stated MIT terms to redistribute description assets.

Users obtain vendor inputs directly under the vendor's terms and stage them with
[scripts/fetch_vendor_assets.py](scripts/fetch_vendor_assets.py). Local inputs and
generated vendor-derived outputs are ignored. Conversion tooling and first-party
ROS wrappers remain here.

**Git history still contains the removed files, as far back as the initial commit
49904d2 on 2026-05-26. A public visibility change exposes that history. No history
rewrite has been performed.**

## Synria Robotics

Source: [Synria-Robot-Descriptions](https://github.com/Synria-Robotics/Synria-Robot-Descriptions),
including the Alicia-D v5.6 URDF and STL meshes.

The recorded 2026-05-27 vendor correspondence described RoboCore and Alicia-SDK ROS
repositories as primarily MIT, with redistribution permitted and attribution
required. The recorded robot-description `pyproject.toml` classifier instead
identifies GPL-3. The scope and discrepancy remain unresolved; no license
equivalence is asserted here. The prior file set is recorded in the removal
manifest. First-party xacro wrappers are distinct from the removed vendor URDF.

## Yahboom Technology

Sources: [ROSMASTER-M3PRO](https://github.com/YahboomTechnology/ROSMASTER-M3PRO)
and the [product study page](https://www.yahboom.net/study/ROSMASTER-M3PRO)
Code-Firmware archive, also distributed through vendor support and the robot's
onboard filesystem.

The integration record reports no vendor redistribution terms: the description
package declares `TODO: License declaration`; the MoveIt package's BSD entry is
a Setup Assistant template. The 2026-05-27 support correspondence did not address
licensing. This notice does not infer permission.

The first-party fetch script retains the documented fix to the two
`arm_base_Link.STL` references: `dofbot_M3Pro_descripton` becomes
`yahboom_M3Pro_description`. Other vendor joint names, including
`arm4_Joiint`, remain unchanged.

Bundled upstream packages OrbbecSDK_ROS2, imu_tools and ira_laser_tools were not
imported into this repository. Users obtain any required runtime packages
separately under their own terms.

